1.7 Added support for extended Adaptive Biasing Force (eABF) method
    Developer: Steven L. Austin and H. Lee Woodcock
    Institution: University of South Florida
    Date: July, 2024

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/243
Git commit: ab68eb47

Description:
The extended adaptive biasing force (eABF) method is an enhanced sampling method designed to enable repetitive sampling of conformational transitions. With eABF, prohibitive energy barriers are effectively flattened by the application of a biasing force along a targeted collective variable (CV), for instance, along the root mean squared displacement (RMSD) of the protein backbone, to promote transitions to and from a reference structure (such as a crystal state).

prefx Keys: EABF

