1.13 Bugfix for NTOT > 2^28 fatal error
     Developer: Rick Venable
     Institution: NIH/NHLBI
     Date: April 11, 2024

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/249
Git commit: c127c930

Description:
Memory allocation was changed in correl.F90 to avoid a seg fault when computing
a correlation function with more 2^28 or more input data points.
The large space_sf array with pointers was replaced by allocation of some or
all of the six arrays as needed.

Calculation of correlation functions with more than 2^28 data points in
the input time series triggers a fatal error. Changing
the memory allocation scheme from a single large array with six pointers
to one which allocates each array separately resolved the problem.
CORFUN can now compute C(t) for an input time series with 300,000,000 points.

Sample input to reproduce the problem (or testcase):
Read a time series with 268,435,456 or more points, and attempt the CORFUN
command above. Results in the error--

CORREL>    corfun pxy pxy total @MXC nonorm
Parameter: MXC -> "5000000"
forrtl: severe (174): SIGSEGV, segmentation fault occurred

Files Involved: source/correl/correl.F90

1.14 Toppar updates 2024
     Developer: Alex MacKerell
     Institution: University of Maryland, Baltimore
     Date: 1 August 2024

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/250
