2.10 Variable e14fac
     Developer: Charles L. Brooks III
     Institution: University of Michigan
     Date: 11 October 2024

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/260
Git commit: e09d5e92

Description:
In order to enable the use of e14fac values that differ within your system,
e.g., if you wanted to run gaff ligands or LigParGen ligands with c36
proteins this functionality utilizes an NATOM array set-up in scalar with
scalar e14f set <value> <selection>
that is then propgated to OpenMM's MD engine or BLaDE for energy or
dynamics calls.
If a fixed constant e14fac value is to be used, OpenMM and BLaDE now use
the same NATOM array of e14ff values, but all values are the same.
We note that this option is presently only accessible in the CHARMM/BLaDE API
and the CHARMM/OpenMM API.
VARIABLE E14FAC VALUES ARE NOT SUPPORTED ON OTHER CHARMM ENERGY ROUTINES

