==============================================================================
[3] c50b1 Change Log

     At the 2025 CHARMM meeting (Florida State University
July 18-20, 2025), we decided to release CHARMM c50b1 incorporating
enhancements and fixes from the developmental c50a1 and c50a2 versions into
the stable version.

The c50b1 release includes the following enhancements and fixes from the
developmental versions c50a1 and c50a2 during the development period of
August 15, 2024 through August 15, 2025. These have been added to the
stable version c49b2 to create the stable version c50b1.

3.1 kernn module with associated test from Silvan Kaeser is added to CHARMM
    Developer: Silvan Kaeser, Markus Meuwly
    Institution: University of Basel
    Date: 12.7.2024

Merge request: https://charmm-dev.org:1976/bucknerj/dev-release/-/merge_requests/241
Git commit: 1d191d78

Description:
The KerNN module is geared towards efficient and high-quality intramolecular
interactions for polyatomic molecules in CHARMM. This is achieved by
replacing the CHARMM bonded contributions with predictions (energies and forces)
from a small neural network (NN). The module is intended to be used for gas-phase
spectroscopic studies and reactive dynamics or as a driver of the intramolecular
contributions in condensed-phase simulations.

